B.Hg=new A.aa("prints","Prints on the Urn","",0,"Three sets of prints came up under the powder. On the lid, Penny Cotta's: she fills it every morning. On the left handle, Tira Misu's. On the right handle, Graham Cracker's.",B.c9,B.cK,null,B.t,B.e,"churlock")
B.MH=s(["penny","tira","graham"],t.s)
B.Q3={watch:0,clock:1,boots:2,chart:3,cellarbook:4,ovenlog:5,extension:6,souffle:7,phone:8,urn:9,tracks:10,wetprints:11,newwill:12,solicitor:13,planner:14,silver:15,candles:16,gloves:17,tickets:18,note:19,notepad:20,tally:21,prints:22}
B.Ph=new A.ba(B.Q3,[u.Q,u.Q,u.o,"Splendid. Now all we want is the weapon.",u.h,u.p,u.X,u.N,"The operator's own record. I should call that one alibi we need not worry about.","I tried to lift it. I could not. I should like to know how many hands it took, and the sergeant has a chart for that.",u.D,u.D,u.F,u.F,"Tell them afterwards, not before. So she feared what they might do if they knew. Did they know?","Then what were they doing in there for an hour? Ask the one who works on the other side of that wall.","Then what were they doing in there for an hour, in the dark? Ask the one who works on the other side of that wall.","Soaked right through, not splashed. That is no spilled cup.","One way, for tonight, and two of them. People who mean to come back buy returns.","Unsigned, but paper has a way of telling you where it came from. Whose pad is that?","Now why would a butler tear off that one sheet? Ask him. Then see whether his answer fits the hour.","I never trust a total I have not added up myself.","Three sets. One of them belongs there. Ask the other two what business they had with it, and then ask the housekeeper whether it is true."],t.li)
B.N_=s(["First, how was it done? Look hard at that urn, and at whatever tracks lead away from it. Could one dessert have managed it alone?","If it took two, look for two who were together. The telephone log, the souffl\xe9 and the boots each put one dessert somewhere alone. Who does that leave?","Their story is the silver. Go and stand in the dining room. Look at the cabinet, the candles, the notepad. Then ask Penny what she heard through the wall.","Find out what was to be signed this morning, and who stood to lose by it. And add up that tally sheet yourself, Churlock."],t.s)
B.Q4={sprinkles:0,glaze:1,penny:2,graham:3,tira:4,cannoli:5,barry:6}
B.a3L=new A.M("what","What happened to her?","Victim is Mrs. \xc9claire Senclair, founder of Senclair Confections. Somebody drenched her, Detective \u2014 gallons of scalding espresso, poured until she went soggy and simply fell apart. We outlined what was left in powdered sugar.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.a2v=new A.M("weapon","What was the weapon?","That brass espresso urn lying on its side. Take a good look at it.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.Nf=s(["urn"],t.s)
B.a3u=new A.M("weight","How heavy is that urn?","Full? Glaze and I tried to right it between us and nearly lost our icing. I had a go on my own first. Couldn't get one side off the floor.",B.Nf,B.e,null)
B.K2=s([B.a3L,B.a2v,B.a3u,B.l6,B.lk],t.q)
B.a2j=new A.M("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Strict, but fair. She'd been upset lately \u2014 her pearls went missing last month, and she'd been shut up with her solicitor ever since.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.a2V=new A.M("suspect","Who do you suspect?","I don't like to stir the pot... but the Colonel owes Madam a fortune, and Barry was in her bad books over the strawberries.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.fr=s(["graham/where"],t.s)
B.a2P=new A.M("dark","Graham says he and Tira were counting silver next door.","Last night? The dining room is right through that wall, Detective. From half ten on it was dark and silent as a fridge. No light under the door, not a clink. And you can't count a hundred and forty-four pieces of silver without a clink.",B.e,B.fr,null)
B.ot=s(["graham/dark"],t.s)
B.a3G=new A.M("lamp","Graham says they worked by a shaded lamp.","A lamp? The only lamp on this floor is the one on my kitchen table, and it never left my sight. I was reading my basting times by it.",B.e,B.ot,null)
B.oE=s(["silver"],t.s)
B.a3J=new A.M("silver","Your tag says you counted the silver at 3 PM.","Every piece, and polished it too. It's counted on the first of the month, and that was yesterday afternoon. Nobody had any call to count it again that night.",B.oE,B.e,null)
B.om=s(["candles"],t.s)
B.a2Q=new A.M("candles",u.b,"I should think not, I only put them in yesterday afternoon. Still white, are they? Then nobody has had a light on in that room since.",B.om,B.e,null)
B.a2f=new A.M("cocoa","Did Tira fetch port from the cellar at nine?","She did, that much is true. Whether nine was the only time she went down, I couldn't tell you. I had my head in an oven.",B.jJ,B.e,null)
B.a3a=new A.M("boom","Could you hear the Colonel on the telephone?","Hear him? The whole county could. He was bellowing about the Battle of Blancmange for the best part of an hour. It came down the stairwell like a brass band.",B.e,B.og,null)
B.N0=s(["graham/prints"],t.s)
B.a2M=new A.M("carry","Does Graham carry the urn to the breakfast table?","That urn? It hasn't left its stand in twenty years, Detective. I fill the coffee pot from it and carry the pot. Nobody carries the urn anywhere. Nobody could.",B.e,B.N0,null)
B.Nc=s([B.lj,B.a2j,B.a2V,B.a2P,B.a3G,B.a3J,B.a2Q,B.a2f,B.a3a,B.a2M,B.Aj,B.la,B.Ak,B.lg,B.lf,B.ll],t.q)
B.a36=new A.M("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","In the dining room, sir, conducting the silver inventory with Miss Tira's kind assistance. Half past ten until half past eleven. One hundred and forty-four pieces, all present.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.a3d=new A.M("suspect","Who do you suspect?","It is not a butler's place to speculate, sir. I will observe only that the Colonel is deeply in debt to Madam.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.oe=s(["penny/dark"],t.s)
B.a2l=new A.M("dark",u.E,"We worked by a single shaded lamp, sir, so as not to disturb the house. And one lays silver down on baize. It makes no sound.",B.e,B.oe,null)
B.a2t=new A.M("silver","Penny had already counted the silver at 3 PM.","Mrs. Cotta counts, sir. I verify. It is the difference between a housekeeper and a butler.",B.oE,B.e,null)
B.a3h=new A.M("candles",u.b,"As I say, sir, we did not use the chandelier. One does not burn Madam's good candles to count spoons.",B.om,B.e,null)
B.MA=s(["notepad"],t.s)
B.a3e=new A.M("notepad","What did you write on the missing sheet?","A reminder to wind the hall clock, sir. Tonight, at eleven. It keeps poor time if one is late.",B.MA,B.e,null)
B.oz=s(["note"],t.s)
B.a2x=new A.M("note","This burnt note is on your monogrammed paper.","Madam's paper, sir, not mine. There is a pad of it in every room of this house. Anyone might have used it.",B.oz,B.e,null)
B.oy=s(["newwill","solicitor"],t.s)
B.a37=new A.M("will","She was dismissing you without a pension.","Madam said nothing of the kind to me, sir. One would naturally be distressed, after thirty years.",B.oy,B.e,null)
B.oH=s(["tickets"],t.s)
B.a2L=new A.M("tickets","Two tickets to Biscotti Bay, Graham?","A holiday, sir, long planned. Miss Tira dislikes queues and asked me to purchase her ticket along with my own. That is all.",B.oH,B.e,null)
B.oB=s(["pearls"],t.s)
B.a3g=new A.M("pearls","What happened to the Senclair pearls?","Mislaid, sir. Madam was forever mislaying things. I could not say how a pawn ticket came to be in the case.",B.oB,B.e,null)
B.H7=new A.aa("tally","Silver Tally Sheet","",0,"The sheet Graham says he and Tira filled in last night: \u201cForks, 48. Knives, 48. Spoons, 50. Total, 144 pieces, all present. Counted 10:30 to 11:30 PM. Signed, G. Cracker and T. Misu.\u201d",B.cP,B.a0,null,B.t,B.e,"graham")
B.a2S=new A.M("tally","Is there any record of your silver count?","Certainly, sir. Our tally sheet from last night, signed by Miss Tira and myself. I trust that settles the matter.",B.e,B.fr,B.H7)
B.a2C=new A.M("prints","Your fingerprints are on the urn.","I carry that urn to the breakfast table daily, sir. With assistance. One would expect to find them.",B.dN,B.e,null)
B.M9=s([B.a36,B.l9,B.a3d,B.a2l,B.a2t,B.a3h,B.a3e,B.a2x,B.a37,B.a2L,B.a3g,B.a2S,B.a2C,B.l7,B.lb,B.l8,B.lh],t.q)
B.a38=new A.M("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","Helping Graham count the silver in the dining room, darling. Half ten to half eleven. Frightfully dull \u2014 spoons, spoons, spoons.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.a2i=new A.M("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Aunt \xc9claire was a sweet old thing with a very hard glaze. We adored each other. Everyone knows I am her sole heir.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.a2A=new A.M("suspect","Who do you suspect?","The Colonel, darling. He owes her mountains of sugar. Or that muddy little gardener she was about to sack.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.a2p=new A.M("dark",u.E,"Penny had her head in an oven, darling. She wouldn't have noticed a brass band marching through the hall.",B.e,B.oe,null)
B.a2H=new A.M("lamp","Where did the lamp you worked by come from?","Lamp? We had the chandelier blazing, darling, one can't count spoons in the gloom. ...Why, what did Graham say?",B.e,B.ot,null)
B.Mc=s(["gloves"],t.s)
B.a3z=new A.M("gloves","Your gloves are soaked in espresso.","I spilled my after-dinner coffee, darling. All of it. I'm a tiramisu; we're practically made of coffee. I hid them because Auntie paid for them and would have shrieked.",B.Mc,B.e,null)
B.a3s=new A.M("will","Your aunt was cutting you out of her will.","Auntie rewrote her will every time her bunions ached, darling, and tore it up again by Friday. Nobody took it seriously. Least of all me.",B.oy,B.e,null)
B.a3w=new A.M("tickets","You have a train ticket to Biscotti Bay for tonight.","A little seaside air, darling, for my nerves. Graham queued for me. Is a girl not allowed a holiday?",B.oH,B.e,null)
B.a3x=new A.M("pearls","What happened to the Senclair pearls?","Auntie lost them, found them, lost them again. I never touched the ugly things.",B.oB,B.e,null)
B.a3n=new A.M("prints","Your fingerprints are on the urn.","I helped Graham move it on Sunday, darling, when the footman was off. Once. It was frightfully heavy and I broke a nail.",B.dN,B.e,null)
B.KG=s([B.a38,B.a2i,B.a2A,B.a2p,B.a2H,B.a3z,B.a3s,B.a3w,B.a3x,B.l3,B.a3n,B.lm],t.q)
B.a3b=new A.M("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","On the telephone on the attic landing, sir! Ten to eleven until half past, swapping war stories with old Major Meringue at the Fort Fondant Officers' Club.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.Ad=new A.M("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","\xc9claire? Splendid woman. Very patient with a chap's temporary financial embarrassments.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.a2h=new A.M("suspect","Who do you suspect?","The housekeeper found the body, sir. In my experience the chap who finds the body wants watching. Or the gardener. Never trust a tart.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.a2u=new A.M("dining","Did you pass the dining room last night?","Came down the stairs at half past eleven when I rang off, sir, straight past it. Door shut, no light under it, quiet as a churchyard. Why, was somebody meant to be in there?",B.e,B.fr,null)
B.jM=s(["ricottadrip"],t.s)
B.a2m=new A.M("drip","There is ricotta on the floor by the telephone.","I stood on that spot for forty minutes, sir. A chap drips. Old war wound. I'd be more worried if there were none.",B.jM,B.e,null)
B.ou=s(["iou"],t.s)
B.Al=new A.M("iou","You owed her 50,000 sugar cubes.","I did, and I do, and I'm not proud of it. But she had given me until Christmas, and a dead creditor's heirs are far less patient. Her death is the worst thing that could happen to my finances, what!",B.ou,B.e,null)
B.GI=new A.aa("extension","Mrs. Senclair's Note","",0,"A note the Colonel says Mrs. Senclair wrote him last week: \u201cMy dear Colonel, do not trouble yourself about the sugar. Take until Christmas. Your friend, \xc9claire Senclair.\u201d",B.bW,B.a0,null,B.t,B.e,"cannoli")
B.A6=new A.M("proof","Can you prove she gave you more time?",u.v,B.ou,B.e,B.GI)
B.N3=s(["sabre"],t.s)
B.A7=new A.M("sabre","Your sabre is in the attic, and it is sticky.","Toffee apples, sir! Fearsome things to slice. I was carving one for myself on Sunday, the blade stuck fast in that dummy, and I haven't had the puff to pull it out since.",B.N3,B.e,null)
B.Mq=s([B.a3b,B.Ad,B.a2h,B.a2u,B.a2m,B.Al,B.A6,B.l4,B.A7],t.q)
B.a3F=new A.M("suspect","Who do you suspect?","Couldn't say, guv. But whoever it was had a strong back. I haul coal all day and I can't shift that coffee urn on me own.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.a3H=new A.M("furnace","I pulled a burnt note out of your furnace.","Ain't my writin', guv \u2014 I can barely spell \u201cfertiliser\u201d. But when I came in at midnight the furnace door was open and the fire fresh-poked. I banked it meself at six. Somebody had been at it.",B.oz,B.e,null)
B.K8=s([B.A8,B.l5,B.a3F,B.a3H,B.ln,B.lc,B.le,B.ld,B.li],t.q)
B.Pa=new A.ba(B.Q4,[B.K2,B.ok,B.Nc,B.M9,B.KG,B.Mq,B.K8],t.wU)
B.MG=s(["penny","cannoli","barry"],t.s)
B.PA=new A.oP("brew","A Bitter Brew",B.WC,B.Nm,B.Lk,B.No,B.WF,B.Hg,B.MH,"1892",B.Ph,B.N_,B.Pa,"Mrs. Senclair was about to sign a new will, cutting off her niece Tira and dismissing Graham without a pension for helping Tira pawn her pearls. The espresso urn is too heavy for one dessert, so it took two \u2014 and while Penny, the Colonel and Barry can each be placed elsewhere by something independent, Tira and Graham vouch only for one another. Their silver inventory never happened: the dining room was dark and silent all evening. At eleven Tira lured her aunt downstairs while Graham fetched the urn, and together they tipped it. The tally sheet they signed was written afterwards, in a hurry: its forks, knives and spoons add up to 146, not 144.",B.MG)
B.Q7={penny:0}
B.WB=new A.d3(B.Q7,1,t.fF)
B.Gx=new A.aa("tin","Empty Cake Tin","pantry",1,"A large tin on the pantry shelf labelled \u201cSenclair Christmas Fruitcake \u2014 12 years old. DO NOT EAT.\u201d The tin is empty. A ring in the dust shows it was lifted down very recently.",B.nV,B.i1,null,B.t,B.e,null)
B.Hf=new A.aa("scoresheet","Chess Scoresheet","parlor",0,"Graham's meticulous record of last night's game. A move is entered every two or three minutes from 10:32 until 11:58 without a break, each one initialled by both players.",B.nR,B.a0,null,B.t,B.e,null)
B.N2=s(["Eggs: a fresh dozen","came today.","Order none."],t.s)
B.Hc=new A.aa("notepad","Butler's Notepad","dining",0,"Graham's household notepad. The top sheet is gone, but the rubbing raises what was written on it: \u201cEggs: a fresh dozen came today. Order none.\u201d A shopping note.",B.jB,B.a0,null,B.fM,B.N2,null)
B.GO=new A.aa("planner","Appointment Book","study",0,"Mrs. Senclair's appointment book, kept under lock. Today's page: \u201c9 AM, the agency sends the new housekeeper. Tell P.C. after breakfast, not before.\u201d",B.jy,B.a0,"desk",B.t,B.e,null)
B.MQ=s([B.Gx,B.jn,B.jk,B.nE,B.Hf,B.Hc,B.GO],t.F)
B.Gw=new A.aa("underdrip","Sauce Beneath the Body","cellar",1,"The officers marked this where they lifted the remains: a drop of red berry sauce on the flagstones UNDERNEATH where Mrs. Senclair lay. It was on the floor before she fell on it.",B.ca,B.c4,null,B.t,B.e,null)
B.Eg=new A.h(1,0.5568627450980392,0.1411764705882353,0.12549019607843137,B.c)
B.GN=new A.aa("drydrip","Dried Sauce Drip","cellar",2,"A drop of red berry sauce beside the outline, dried to a dark, cracked crust. The drips at the top of the stairs from this morning would still be glossy; this one is hours older.",B.ca,B.Eg,null,B.t,B.e,null)
B.Nt=s([B.Gw,B.GN],t.F)
B.Im=new A.ai(984312,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.DG=new A.h(1,1,0.9529411764705882,0.8784313725490196,B.c)
B.GR=new A.aa("eggs","Egg Basket","kitchen",4,"The egg basket on the counter, with yesterday's delivery slip: \u201c1 dozen, fresh.\u201d All twelve eggs are still in it. A Needy Souffl\xe9 takes six.",B.Im,B.DG,null,B.t,B.e,null)
B.HS=new A.ai(57994,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.Gt=new A.aa("ovenash","Cold Oven","kitchen",2,"The kitchen oven. The firebox holds nothing but old grey ash, cold right through, and the coal scuttle beside it is full to the brim.",B.HS,B.ih,null,B.t,B.e,null)
B.MS=s([B.GR,B.Gt],t.F)
B.Ll=s(["Please send a modern housekeeper at once.","The present one, P. Cotta,","is to be retired","without notice or pension.","She makes the same puddings as ever."],t.s)
B.GC=new A.aa("retire","Letter to an Agency","study",0,"On Mrs. Senclair's desk, ready to post: \u201cPlease send a modern housekeeper at once. The present one, P. Cotta, is to be retired without notice or pension. She makes the same puddings she made thirty years ago.\u201d",B.bW,B.a0,null,B.fN,B.Ll,null)
B.JW=s([B.jp,B.GC],t.F)
B.He=new A.aa("cakesack","Christmas Fruitcake","pantry",3,"Pushed deep into a flour sack: a fruitcake as hard as granite. One corner is freshly chipped, and there is custard on it. It wants dusting for fingerprints.",B.by,B.aL,"sacks",B.t,B.e,null)
B.GX=new A.aa("cakecrate","Christmas Fruitcake","storage",1,"At the bottom of a crate of old curtains: a fruitcake as hard as granite. One corner is freshly chipped, and there is custard on it. It wants dusting for fingerprints.",B.by,B.aL,"crates",B.t,B.e,null)
B.KU=s([B.He,B.GX],t.F)
B.Lw=s([B.jF,B.Nt,B.MS,B.JW,B.KU],t.Rt)
B.GS=new A.aa("regiment","Letter from the Regiment","study",5,"In the desk drawer, a reply to Mrs. Senclair from Fort Fondant: \u201cMadam, we regret that we can find no record of any Colonel Cannoli among our fighting officers, nor of the medals you describe.\u201d",B.bW,B.a0,"desk",B.t,B.e,null)
B.Gy=new A.aa("ricottadrip","White Cream Drips","entrance",4,"A few spots of thick white ricotta on the floor at the top of the cellar steps, dried at the edges.",B.ca,B.i,null,B.t,B.e,null)
B.Kl=s([B.nF,B.nC,B.nG,B.GS,B.jo,B.jq,B.jt,B.jm,B.jj,B.jl,B.ju,B.nB,B.js,B.ji,B.jr,B.Gy],t.F)
B.PZ={cakesack:0,cakecrate:1}
B.WP=new A.d3(B.PZ,2,t.fF)
B.GE=new A.aa("prints","Prints on the Fruitcake","",0,"Only one dessert's prints came up on the fruitcake: Penny Cotta's. They are sharp and greasy. But then she baked it, twelve years ago, and it has sat in her pantry ever since. There are no others at all.",B.c9,B.cK,null,B.t,B.e,"churlock")
B.ME=s(["penny"],t.s)
B.Qa={watch:0,clock:1,boots:2,chart:3,cellarbook:4,ovenlog:5,extension:6,phone:7,souffle:8,tin:9,scoresheet:10,underdrip:11,drydrip:12,eggs:13,ovenash:14,recipe:15,retire:16,planner:17,cakesack:18,cakecrate:19,notepad:20,prints:21}
B.P8=new A.ba(B.Qa,[u.Q,u.Q,u.o,"Splendid. Now all we want is the weapon.",u.h,u.p,u.X,u.B,"Everybody else's alibi is somebody's word. This one is a pudding. Can a pudding lie, Churlock?","Somebody lifted that down who knew just where it was kept. Mind you, in this house, that is everyone.","No gaps at all, and each man watching the other. Can anyone outside that room say the same of them?","Timing, Churlock. When did that get there? Officer Glaze handled the body. Ask him.","Timing, Churlock. When did that get there? Officer Glaze knows how such things dry. Ask him.","A souffl\xe9 takes eggs. Count them again. Then ask her where hers came from.","Cold, and the coal untouched. Barry fills that scuttle. Ask him how much an hour's baking burns.","Thirty years is a long time to be owed. But she had waited thirty years already. Why last night, of all nights?","So that is what was coming. The question is whether the housekeeper knew it was coming.","Tell her after breakfast. So today was to be the day. Did she know?",u.f,u.f,"A shopping note. But notice what it says about the larder, Churlock.","Sharp, you say? After twelve years in a tin? Ask Officer Glaze how long a print stays sharp."],t.li)
B.LP=s(["Start with the clock, Churlock. When did she die? And then: who can show where they were, with something better than their own say-so?","The chess players vouch for each other, which is worth little, unless somebody else heard them. Ask Miss Tira what came up the stairs while she was on the telephone.","That leaves one alibi which is not a person at all. Go back to the kitchen. Look at the oven, the eggs, the coal. Ask Barry what he saw through the window.","Now the cellar floor. Something was dropped there, and it matters very much when. Ask Officer Glaze. And read that oven log against the time of death."],t.s)
B.a2W=new A.M("what","What happened to her?","Victim is Mrs. \xc9claire Senclair, founder of Senclair Confections. Struck from behind, once, with something heavy. She went down like a dropped tray. We traced where she fell in powdered sugar.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.a3l=new A.M("weapon","What was the weapon?","Dense, blunt, about the size of a brick. We picked raisins and candied peel out of the, er, point of impact. Fruitcake, Detective. An old one. One dessert could swing it.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.LD=s([B.a2W,B.a3l,B.l6,B.lk],t.q)
B.Nd=s(["underdrip"],t.s)
B.a2F=new A.M("under","There was sauce underneath the body.","I noted that myself when we moved her. Whatever dripped there, dripped before she hit the floor, or as she did. Nobody slid it under her afterwards.",B.Nd,B.e,null)
B.LM=s(["drydrip"],t.s)
B.a2X=new A.M("dry","How long does berry sauce take to dry like that?","Fresh sauce stays tacky a couple of hours. That spot was bone dry and cracked when we arrived at seven, and the housekeeper says she only came down at half six.",B.LM,B.e,null)
B.a3c=new A.M("fresh","Would twelve-year-old fingerprints still be sharp?","After twelve years in a tin? They'd be dull as dust, Detective, if they came up at all. Sharp and greasy means fresh. Hours old, not years.",B.dN,B.e,null)
B.Ku=s([B.Ap,B.Ac,B.Af,B.Aa,B.a2F,B.a2X,B.a3c],t.q)
B.Ne=s(["underdrip","drydrip"],t.s)
B.a2k=new A.M("sauce","There is red berry sauce beside the body.","Well, of course it is. I told you \u2014 I went all to pieces when I found her this morning, and my topping runs when I'm upset.",B.Ne,B.e,null)
B.Na=s(["tin"],t.s)
B.a2N=new A.M("tin","The Christmas fruitcake is gone from its tin.","Gone? Twelve years that thing has sat up there. Madam wouldn't let me throw it out. Well, the pantry is never locked, Detective. Anybody could have reached it down.",B.Na,B.e,null)
B.LQ=s(["eggs"],t.s)
B.a2s=new A.M("eggs","All twelve of yesterday's eggs are still in the basket.","I used up last week's eggs first. Waste not, want not.",B.LQ,B.e,null)
B.oA=s(["ovenash"],t.s)
B.a2K=new A.M("oven","Your oven is stone cold and the coal has not been touched.","I always sweep out the grate the moment I've finished baking. And I had coal left over from the day before. Habit, Detective.",B.oA,B.e,null)
B.KP=s(["barry/window"],t.s)
B.a3r=new A.M("window","Barry says the kitchen was empty at eleven.","Barry was half frozen and seeing things. I may have stepped into the scullery for sugar. For a moment.",B.e,B.KP,null)
B.KI=s(["tira/smell"],t.s)
B.a3D=new A.M("smell","Tira says there was no smell of baking last night.","Miss Tira had a telephone pressed to one side of her head and the Colonel's cigar up the other. I shouldn't rely on her nose.",B.e,B.KI,null)
B.MX=s(["retire"],t.s)
B.a3m=new A.M("retire","She was going to retire you without notice.","Was she? She said nothing to me. Thirty years, and the same puddings \u2014 well. They were good enough to build her a factory.",B.MX,B.e,null)
B.a33=new A.M("prints","Your fingerprints are on the fruitcake.","My prints, on my own cake, from my own pantry? I baked the thing, Detective. I'd be more surprised if you'd found the Colonel's.",B.dN,B.e,null)
B.GA=new A.aa("ovenlog","Oven Log","",0,"Penny's oven log card for last night, in pencil: \u201cNeedy Souffl\xe9. IN 10:30. Basted every 2 min. 11:20 \u2014 Madam rang down to say it smelt divine. OUT 11:30. Risen four inches. Eggs: 6.\u201d",B.cP,B.a0,null,B.t,B.e,"penny")
B.a2w=new A.M("log","May I see your oven log?",u.r,B.oF,B.e,B.GA)
B.M8=s([B.lj,B.An,B.Ag,B.a2k,B.a2N,B.a2s,B.a2K,B.a3r,B.a3D,B.a3m,B.a33,B.a2w,B.la,B.lg,B.lf,B.ll],t.q)
B.a2E=new A.M("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","In the parlor, sir, at chess with the Colonel, from half past ten until midnight. Neither of us left the board.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.a2U=new A.M("sheet","Your scoresheet shows no breaks at all.","Every move timed and initialled by both players, sir. The Colonel insists upon it, as he believes that I cheat. I believe the same of him. It makes for an honest record.",B.fs,B.e,null)
B.Kd=s(["penny/eggs"],t.s)
B.a2r=new A.M("eggs","Would Penny bake with last week's eggs?","Mrs. Cotta, sir? Never. There were no eggs left from last week; I signed for the new dozen yesterday because the larder was bare. And she permits nothing but the freshest. She says a souffl\xe9 knows.",B.e,B.Kd,null)
B.a2O=new A.M("brandy","There is ricotta at the top of the cellar steps.","The Colonel fetched up his own brandy at eight o'clock, sir, rather than ring for me. I disapproved, and entered it in the cellar book.",B.jM,B.e,null)
B.KK=s([B.a2E,B.l9,B.Ae,B.a2U,B.a2r,B.a2O,B.l7,B.lb,B.l8,B.lh],t.q)
B.a3j=new A.M("sheet","You initialled every move on Graham's scoresheet.","Had to, sir. The fellow moves his bishops when one blinks. Never took my eyes off him in an hour and a half. He'll tell you the same of me, the cheek of it.",B.fs,B.e,null)
B.a2J=new A.M("drip","You left ricotta at the top of the cellar steps.","Went down for a decent brandy at eight, sir. Graham pours like a miser. \xc9claire was alive and well and telling me so at supper.",B.jM,B.e,null)
B.MW=s(["regiment"],t.s)
B.a2q=new A.M("regiment","Fort Fondant has never heard of you.","Not among the FIGHTING officers, no. I was a colonel in the Catering Corps, sir. Forty years of trifle for the troops. One doesn't advertise it. \xc9claire knew, and teased me rotten.",B.MW,B.e,null)
B.L_=s([B.Ao,B.Ad,B.Ah,B.a3j,B.a2J,B.Al,B.A6,B.l4,B.a2q,B.A7],t.q)
B.a3B=new A.M("suspect","Who do you suspect?","Graham and the Colonel, darling, thick as thieves over that chessboard. Each one swears the other never moved. How convenient.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.a3i=new A.M("check","Could the chess players have slipped out?","I only wish they had, darling. The Colonel bellowed \u201cCHECK!\u201d up the stairwell every few minutes the whole time I was on the telephone, and Graham sniffed after every one. It was like a metronome. Neither of them drew breath long enough to murder anyone.",B.e,B.fr,null)
B.oj=s(["penny/where"],t.s)
B.a2T=new A.M("smell","Penny was baking a souffl\xe9 at that hour.","Was she? How odd. When Penny bakes, the whole stairwell reeks of it for hours. Last night I smelt nothing but the Colonel's cigar.",B.e,B.oj,null)
B.K9=s([B.A9,B.Ai,B.a3B,B.a3i,B.a2T,B.Ab,B.Am,B.l3,B.lm],t.q)
B.a2B=new A.M("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","Out in the greenhouse 'til midnight, coverin' the strawberries against the frost. Came up to the house the once, about eleven, after me tea flask, but the door was latched so I went back. Penny let me in at midnight.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.a2y=new A.M("suspect","Who do you suspect?","That Colonel owes her a packet, and Miss Tira gets the lot. Take your pick, guv.",B.e,B.e,null)
B.a3v=new A.M("window","Penny says she never left her oven.","Does she? When I came up at eleven I looked in the kitchen window, hopin' she'd pass me flask out. Lamp lit, oven dark, no Penny. I stood there a good five minutes. Thought she'd gone to bed.",B.e,B.oj,null)
B.a3o=new A.M("coal","The kitchen coal scuttle is still full.","'Course it is, I filled it at six like every evenin'. If it's still full this mornin', nobody's fired that oven. An hour's bakin' burns half of it.",B.oA,B.e,null)
B.Kv=s(["penny/oven"],t.s)
B.a2Z=new A.M("leftover","Penny says she had coal left from the day before.","Not a lump, guv. She was scrapin' the bottom when I filled it \u2014 said so herself, and none too kindly.",B.e,B.Kv,null)
B.Mw=s([B.a2B,B.l5,B.a2y,B.a3v,B.a3o,B.a2Z,B.ln,B.lc,B.le,B.ld,B.li],t.q)
B.P3=new A.ba(B.uQ,[B.LD,B.Ku,B.M8,B.KK,B.L_,B.K9,B.Mw],t.wU)
B.Lz=s(["barry","graham","tira","cannoli"],t.s)
B.Pz=new A.oP("cake","The Twelve-Year Fruitcake",B.WB,B.MQ,B.Lw,B.Kl,B.WP,B.GE,B.ME,"1879",B.P8,B.LP,B.P3,"Thirty years ago Mrs. Senclair built her fortune on Penny Cotta's cream puff recipe and never paid her a cube; now she meant to retire Penny without notice. Penny's alibi was a souffl\xe9 \u2014 but it was never baked last night. The oven was cold and the eggs untouched, and Barry saw an empty kitchen at eleven. At 11:05 she struck Mrs. Senclair in the cellar with the rock-hard Christmas fruitcake, leaving a drip of her own sauce beneath the body, then \u201cfound\u201d her in the morning. The chess players were heard throughout, Tira was on the telephone, and Barry was locked outside. The oven log she handed over was written afterwards: it has Madam ringing down at 11:20, a quarter of an hour after she died.",B.Lz)
